{"id":"p08-l12","minutes":40,"summary":"Oversampling is cheap and analogue filters are not, so sample fast and reduce the rate digitally. You derive why decimation needs an anti-aliasing filter first, build a polyphase decimator that computes only the outputs you keep, check it against filter-then-downsample, and verify that out-of-band tones alias by less than the specified level.","html":"<h2 id=\"downsampling-folds-again\">Downsampling folds again</h2>\n<p>Keeping every <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span>-th sample, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>, lowers the rate to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span>, and everything between the new Nyquist <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> and the old one folds back into the band, exactly as analogue sampling did (Phase 07 lesson 16). So first <strong>low-pass to below <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></strong>, then downsample. That’s <strong>decimation</strong>.</p>\n<p>The usual pattern: a cheap RC in front of an ADC sampling at, say, 8× the needed rate, a steep digital FIR, then decimation by 8. The digital filter has exact, repeatable coefficients, and the oversampling also buys resolution (Phase 07 lesson 17).</p>\n<p><strong>Interpolation</strong> is the mirror image: insert <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> zeros between samples, then low-pass to remove the images.</p>\n<h2 id=\"polyphase-don-t-compute-what-you-throw-away\">Polyphase: don’t compute what you throw away</h2>\n<p>Filtering at the high rate and then discarding <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> of every <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> outputs wastes <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> of the work. Split the filter into <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> <strong>polyphase components</strong> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>, and the input into <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> phases <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>. Then</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:3.2316em;vertical-align:-1.4032em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.8283em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.8829em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span><span class=\"mrel mtight\">=</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.3em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.4032em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.8479em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3021em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>Each branch runs at the <em>low</em> rate. The result is identical to filter-then-downsample, at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> of the cost.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"decimate\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A 50 Hz and a 420 Hz tone sampled at 1 kHz, decimated by M. Without the filter, 420 Hz folds into the new band; with it, the alias is buried.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>Decimate from 8 kHz to 1 kHz (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">8</span></span></span></span>) keeping 0–400 Hz with aliases below −60 dB.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>New Nyquist: 500 Hz. Anything at or above <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">400</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">600</span></span></span></span> Hz would alias into the 0–400 Hz band.</li>\n<li>Filter: pass to 400 Hz, stop from 600 Hz, 60 dB. Kaiser (lesson 4): <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">200/8000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.025</span></span></span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">52/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2.285</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.025</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">146</span></span></span></span> taps.</li>\n<li>Direct: 146 multiplies per <em>input</em> sample, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.17</span></span></span></span> M/s. Polyphase: 146 per <em>output</em>, 146 k/s, 8× less.</li>\n<li>A 1 V tone at 1.7 kHz would alias to 300 Hz; after the filter it’s below 1 mV.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">decimate.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> scipy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> signal\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">polyphase_decimate</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">x, h, M</span>):\n    h = np.concatenate([h, np.zeros((-<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(h)) % M)])           <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># pad to a multiple of M</span>\n    K = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(h) // M\n    n_out = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(x) // M\n    y = np.zeros(n_out)\n    xp = np.concatenate([np.zeros(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(h)), x])                   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># history for the start</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> p <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(M):\n        hp = h[p::M]                                             <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># p-th polyphase component</span>\n        <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># branch input: x[mM - p] for m = 0..n_out-1 (offset by the padding)</span>\n        xb = xp[<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(h) - p: <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(h) - p + n_out * M: M]\n        hist = xp[<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(h) - p - (K - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) * M: <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(h) - p: M][:K - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> K &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> np.array([])\n        y += np.convolve(np.concatenate([hist, xb]), hp, mode=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;valid&quot;</span>)[:n_out]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> y\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    fs, M = <span class=\"hljs-number\">8000.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>\n    beta = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1102</span> * (<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span> - <span class=\"hljs-number\">8.7</span>)\n    n_taps = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(np.ceil(<span class=\"hljs-number\">52</span> / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.285</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.025</span>) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)) | <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>\n    h = signal.firwin(n_taps, <span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>, window=(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;kaiser&quot;</span>, beta), fs=fs)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;taps:&quot;</span>, n_taps)\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(<span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span>)\n    x = rng.standard_normal(<span class=\"hljs-number\">8000</span>)\n    y_ref = signal.lfilter(h, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, x)[::M]\n    y = polyphase_decimate(x, h, M)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.allclose(y, y_ref, atol=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># alias check: tones that would fold into 0-400 Hz are attenuated by more than 60 dB</span>\n    t = np.arange(<span class=\"hljs-number\">80_000</span>) / fs\n    worst = -np.inf\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> f <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (<span class=\"hljs-number\">600</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">900</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1700</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2600</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3900</span>):\n        tone = np.sin(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * f * t)\n        out = polyphase_decimate(tone, h, M)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2000</span>:]\n        worst = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(worst, <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span> * np.log10(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(out).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()))\n    inband = polyphase_decimate(np.sin(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * <span class=\"hljs-number\">300</span> * t), h, M)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2000</span>:]\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;worst aliased level <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{worst:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> dB, 300 Hz passes at <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>*np.log10(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(inband).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> dB&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> worst &lt; -<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span> * np.log10(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(inband).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>())) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># without the filter, 1.7 kHz folds onto 300 Hz at full amplitude</span>\n    folded = np.sin(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1700</span> * t)[::M]\n    spec = np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(np.fft.rfft(folded[:<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>])) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(np.argmax(spec) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">300</span>) &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> spec.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Decimating by 64 in one stage needs a very long filter. Why do two stages of 8 help?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The filter length scales with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span>. The first stage can have a wide transition (only aliases into the <em>final</em> band matter, and stage 2 removes the rest), so it’s short; the second runs at 1/8 of the rate, so its long filter costs 8× less per tap. The total work drops by roughly an order of magnitude.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why must interpolation filter <em>after</em> inserting zeros?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Inserting zeros keeps the original spectrum but adds images at multiples of the old sampling rate. The low-pass removes those images, leaving a smooth higher-rate signal, with the gain scaled by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p08-l12\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"downsampling-folds-again","title":"Downsampling folds again"},{"id":"polyphase-don-t-compute-what-you-throw-away","title":"Polyphase: don’t compute what you throw away"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p08-l12-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>New Nyquist frequency in Hz after decimating 8 kHz by 8?</p>\n","explain":"<p>f_s/(2M).</p>\n","answer":500,"tol":0.001,"unit":"Hz"},{"id":"p08-l12-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Lowest input frequency in Hz that aliases into 0–400 Hz after decimating to 1 kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>f_s,new − f_pass.</p>\n","answer":600,"tol":0.001,"unit":"Hz"},{"id":"p08-l12-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Where in Hz does 1.7 kHz land after downsampling to 1 kHz without filtering?</p>\n","explain":"<p>It folds to |1700 − 2000|.</p>\n","answer":300,"tol":0.001,"unit":"Hz"},{"id":"p08-l12-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Work saved by polyphase decimation by M = 8 (factor)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Only kept outputs are computed.</p>\n","answer":8,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p08-l12-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Decimation means…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Filter first, or aliases are permanent.</p>\n","options":["downsample, then filter","low-pass filter, then downsample","insert zeros, then filter","only downsample"],"answer":1},{"id":"p08-l12-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Kaiser length estimate for 60 dB with Δf = 0.025 (before rounding)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>From lesson 4.</p>\n","answer":145.87,"tol":0.002,"unit":""}],"code":[{"file":"decimate.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\nfrom scipy import signal\n\ndef polyphase_decimate(x, h, M):\n    h = np.concatenate([h, np.zeros((-len(h)) % M)])           # pad to a multiple of M\n    K = len(h) // M\n    n_out = len(x) // M\n    y = np.zeros(n_out)\n    xp = np.concatenate([np.zeros(len(h)), x])                   # history for the start\n    for p in range(M):\n        hp = h[p::M]                                             # p-th polyphase component\n        # branch input: x[mM - p] for m = 0..n_out-1 (offset by the padding)\n        xb = xp[len(h) - p: len(h) - p + n_out * M: M]\n        hist = xp[len(h) - p - (K - 1) * M: len(h) - p: M][:K - 1] if K > 1 else np.array([])\n        y += np.convolve(np.concatenate([hist, xb]), hp, mode=\"valid\")[:n_out]\n    return y\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    fs, M = 8000.0, 8\n    beta = 0.1102 * (60 - 8.7)\n    n_taps = int(np.ceil(52 / (2.285 * 2 * np.pi * 0.025) + 1)) | 1\n    h = signal.firwin(n_taps, 500, window=(\"kaiser\", beta), fs=fs)\n    print(\"taps:\", n_taps)\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(12)\n    x = rng.standard_normal(8000)\n    y_ref = signal.lfilter(h, 1, x)[::M]\n    y = polyphase_decimate(x, h, M)\n    assert np.allclose(y, y_ref, atol=1e-12)\n    # alias check: tones that would fold into 0-400 Hz are attenuated by more than 60 dB\n    t = np.arange(80_000) / fs\n    worst = -np.inf\n    for f in (600, 900, 1700, 2600, 3900):\n        tone = np.sin(2 * np.pi * f * t)\n        out = polyphase_decimate(tone, h, M)[2000:]\n        worst = max(worst, 20 * np.log10(np.abs(out).max()))\n    inband = polyphase_decimate(np.sin(2 * np.pi * 300 * t), h, M)[2000:]\n    print(f\"worst aliased level {worst:.1f} dB, 300 Hz passes at {20*np.log10(np.abs(inband).max()):.2f} dB\")\n    assert worst < -60 and abs(20 * np.log10(np.abs(inband).max())) < 0.1\n    # without the filter, 1.7 kHz folds onto 300 Hz at full amplitude\n    folded = np.sin(2 * np.pi * 1700 * t)[::M]\n    spec = np.abs(np.fft.rfft(folded[:1000])) / 500\n    assert abs(np.argmax(spec) - 300) <= 1 and spec.max() > 0.9"}]}